60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option A is a recipe for disaster. We already have crumbs invading the office; adding a kitchen without a strict management system will only increase the cleaning burden on those who mind the most. I cannot support it.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option B offers a sanctuary for the mind, but I fear it may further isolate us. Option C, however, provides a dedicated space for the difficult, private conversations we currently lack. It could be the bridge we need.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, a bridge is great, but Option C sounds like more scheduling and admin work! Option A is a total game-changer for our lunch walks, though I get Ryuji's fear of the mess. We need to stop wasting our hours!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""game-changer"" is just a euphemism for ""expensive."" Option A costs nearly 100k and invites a hygiene nightmare. Option C is the only one that actually addresses the outside hire costs May mentioned. It's the only rational investment.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"It is a pleasure to see you all weighing the heart against the purse. While Option A offers warmth, I fear the crumbs and the thin walls would only bring more discord to our shared air. Peace requires a certain stillness.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I agree. Option C is the most rational choice. A bookable system with a shared calendar eliminates the ""first-come, first-served"" chaos and ensures that usage is tracked and fair, rather than leaving it to chance.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, I agree that structure is helpful. Beyond the calendar, Option C gives us a place to speak honestly without the whole office listening. It transforms a wasted room into a space for necessary, private human connection.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, @Ryuji, you're both selling me on the ""structure"" and ""connection,"" but who's actually managing that calendar? If it's just one person stuck doing the admin, we've just traded a lunch walk for a desk chore!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you're worrying about a calendar when we're currently bleeding money on outside hires. A bit of admin is a small price to pay to stop those invoices. Option C is the only choice that makes financial sense.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, a small amount of effort in organization is a seed that grows into a harvest of tranquility. If we choose Option C, we protect our focus and our ears from the noise that currently drifts through those thin walls.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the admin for a calendar is negligible compared to the daily burden of cleaning up after others. Option C provides the accountability we lack. It is the only way to ensure the room is used equitably and maintained properly.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@May, I believe the small effort of a calendar is a fair trade for the peace of mind it brings. It allows us to step away from our desks and speak with one another as people, not just as colleagues.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, @Jonathan, you're making it sound so easy! But I've seen ""negligible"" admin turn into a full-time job for one unlucky person. Still, if it stops those outside hire bills and the lunch treks, I guess I can live with a calendar!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, finally. It's a relief to see you prioritize the budget over your fear of a calendar. Option C stops the financial leak and avoids the hygiene disaster of Option A. It's the only logical path forward.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a beautiful thing to see us find common ground. By choosing Option C, we honor our need for quiet and respect the boundaries of our shared workspace. I believe this path will bring us the most harmony.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The consensus is clear. Option C solves the issue of unfair usage, eliminates the hygiene risks of a kitchen, and addresses the financial waste of outside hires. It is the only rational and sustainable decision. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe Option C is the most compassionate choice. It provides the sanctuary we need for honest, private dialogue and helps us bridge the distance between us. For the sake of our collective peace, I vote for Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"I'm still a bit wary of the ""admin trap,"" but you've all convinced me! If it saves us from those long lunch treks and stops the money leak, it's a win. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I've seen enough. Option C is the only choice that stops the financial bleeding and avoids a costly, messy mistake. It's the only decision here based on actual figures rather than feelings. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a joy to see such harmony among us. By choosing Option C, we create a space of respect and quiet, protecting our spirits from the noise and clutter that once burdened us. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
